 "CET4-202506-2-Q36": {"anchor":"Unlike whole fruit, fruit juice has most of the fibre removed.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q37": {"anchor":"Another reason for fruit juice's recent popularity is the argument that it can help to remove poisonous or harmful substances from the body.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q38": {"anchor":"Aside from the link to type 2 diabetes, many studies agree that fruit juice is harmful if it contributes to an excess in calories.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q39": {"anchor":"The global fruit and vegetable juices market was valued at $154 billion in 2016 and is expected to grow.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q40": {"anchor":"One way we can improve the effects of fruit juice on our health is making sure we select ripe fruit to retain as much of its goodness as possible, according to Roger Clemens, professor of pharmaceutical sciences at the University of Southern California.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q41": {"anchor":"Diets high in fibre have been linked to a lower risk of developing heart disease, stroke, high blood pressure and diabetes, and it's recommended adults consume 30g per day.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q42": {"anchor":"The paper concluded that foods containing fructose may have some small benefits for long-term blood sugar control when they don't lead to over-consumption of calories.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q43": {"anchor":"\"There are a lot of nutrients contained in the parts of the fruits, such as in apple skins, that are excluded when you juice them,\" says Heather Ferris, a professor of medicine.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q44": {"anchor":"It takes our digestive system a while to break these cells down and for fructose to enter the bloodstream.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q45": {"anchor":"Numerous studies have shown that drinking fruit juice doesn't make us consume any less of other foods throughout the day.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q46": {"anchor":"Science now suggests the right dress may give ourselves the extra edge in our professional and personal lives.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q47": {"anchor":"Science says that the clothes we wear affect our behavior, our mood and even the way we interact with others because of the symbolic meaning that we assign to different types of clothing.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q48": {"anchor":"We also evaluate ourselves based on what we are wearing because of the way they make us feel.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q49": {"anchor":"There's a reason tailored jackets are associated with being 'dressed for success'.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q50": {"anchor":"While a good suit works wonders for our performance in the boardroom, wearing formal wear isn't a great idea when we want to socialize.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q51": {"anchor":"With the rise of pop music, jazz, and electronic music, both opera and classical music started to fade away from the public eye.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q52": {"anchor":"The most major indicator of classical music's importance in society today is the fact that much of the popular music that is currently being produced uses similar beats, harmonies, and melodies (旋律) as those that were used in some of classical music's best works.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q53": {"anchor":"A better example for the relevance of opera and classical music can be seen in the invention of the rock opera.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q54": {"anchor":"Fans of classical music can also tell you that there are few types of music that are more expressive.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-2-Q55": {"anchor":"Classical music and opera are the very foundation of what our modern music is based upon.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-3-Q36": {"anchor":"The exact cause of these phantom traffic jams has long remained a mystery.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-3-Q37": {"anchor":"\"Under reasonable conditions today, you might get 1,800 cars per lane per hour throughput (the volume of traffic passing through),\" he added.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-3-Q38": {"anchor":"Hom has been working on the problem of phantom traffic jams for years, and he has come up with a solution: By splitting the difference between the cars in front and the cars behind, the spacing of cars in a stream of traffic can act as a damper (抑制) on phantom traffic jams.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-3-Q39": {"anchor":"But until those systems become standard, human drivers can help reduce phantom traffic jams simply by not following the car in front so closely.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-3-Q40": {"anchor":"Hom calls this method of vehicle spacing bilateral (双边的) control, and he said it could be achieved with relatively simple modifications to the adaptive cruise control that many new cars already have.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-3-Q41": {"anchor":"\"When caught in such a traffic jam, it is common for drivers to assume that there must be an accident, or construction or something,\" said Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) computer science professor Berthold Hom.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-3-Q42": {"anchor":"The bilateral control approach would include adding rear-facing sensors to determine the distance to the vehicle following a car.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-3-Q43": {"anchor":"These are generally known as \"phantom\" traffic jams, in which dense traffic crawls to a halt for no apparent reason at all.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-3-Q44": {"anchor":"A phantom jam begins when a car in dense traffic slows down even slightly, which causes the car behind that vehicle to slow even more—and the slowing action spreads backward through the lane of traffic like a wave, getting worse the farther it spreads.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-3-Q45": {"anchor":"Since starting his research on phantom traffic jams, Hom has learned that schools of fish and flocks of birds and bats use similar spacing strategies to avoid hitting each other while swimming or flying in densely packed groups.","logic":""},
 "CET4-202506-3-Q46": {"anchor":"Our society places a high value on physical beauty.","logic":""},
